{"nodes": [{"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame03801", "label": "Frame 03801: Infrared View of Radial Feeding Rosettes Around Pan Feeders", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame03801.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2022-02-24T22:03:11", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Monochrome infrared CCTV still, '1080P-IPC-Siren', 2022-02-24 22:03:11. The clearest example in this chunk of the radial 'rosette' geometry: birds arranged spoke-like with bodies pointing outward and heads into each pan feeder, forming near-circular petal patterns around the central and flanking pans. Surrounding floor area is comparatively sparse, making the feeder-attendance signal visually separable from ambient loafing behaviour."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame03801_feeder_rosette_formation", "label": "Radial Feeder Rosette Formation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame03801.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The petal/spoke arrangement of bird bodies radiating outward from a pan centre. This geometry is diagnostic because it is produced by the physical constraint of the circular pan rim rather than by social attraction alone, so counting rosette petals approximates instantaneous feeder occupancy without needing individual identity tracking."}], "edges": [{"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame03801", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02101_overhead_cctv_frame", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame0380